Friend Class in C++

📌 Description

This C++ program demonstrates the use of a Friend Class.

The "Auditor" class is declared as a friend of the "Account" class, allowing it to access the private "balance" member of "Account" directly.

---

🧠 Concepts Used

- Classes and Objects
- Encapsulation
- Private Data Members
- Friend Class
- Constructors
- Controlled Access

---

⚙️ Working

The program works as follows:

1. "Account" contains a private variable "balance".
2. "Auditor" is declared as a friend class using:
   friend class Auditor;
3. Because "Auditor" is a friend of "Account", it can access the private "balance" member directly.
4. The "inspect()" function of "Auditor" displays the account balance.
5. An "Account" object is created with an initial balance of "5000.0".

---

🖥️ Sample Output

Account Balance: 5000

---

🧠 OOP Concept Used

Friend Class

A friend class is a class that is given permission to access the private and protected members of another class.

In this program:

friend class Auditor;

makes "Auditor" a friend of "Account".

Therefore, "Auditor" can directly access the private "balance" member of "Account".

---

🎯 Objective

To understand how a friend class can access the private members of another class while providing controlled access.

